.TH MC1-STATUS-TUNNEL 1 "2026-10-28" "mu2edaq-batch-queues" "Mu2e DAQ Tools"
.SH NAME
mc1-status-tunnel \- ssh tunnel to the MC1 Slurm health status site
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mc1-status-tunnel
.RB [ \-j
.IR user@gateway ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR login ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR localport ]
.RB [ \-H
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR addr:port ]
.RB [ \-o ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The status pages written by
.BR mc1-healthcheck (1)
are served by httpd on the loopback interface of
.B mu2e-mc1-worker-01
only (design decision D26), so no firewall port is open. This script forwards
a local port to that address through the G2 gateway, using Kerberos (GSSAPI)
for both hops:
.PP
.EX
ssh -N -L 8081:127.0.0.1:80 -J mu2eshift@g2gateway01.fnal.gov mu2eshift@mu2e-mc1-worker-01.fnal.gov
.EE
.PP
Then browse
.IR http://localhost:8081/ .
Any account that can log in to worker-01 works for
.BR \-u .
.SH OPTIONS
Options override the environment, which overrides the defaults.
.TP
.BI \-j " user@gateway"
ProxyJump hop. Env
.BR MC1_JUMP ;
default
.BR mu2eshift@g2gateway01.fnal.gov .
.TP
.BI \-u " login"
Login on the controller. Env
.BR MC1_HC_TUNNEL_USER ;
default
.BR mu2eshift .
.TP
.BI \-p " localport"
Local port. Env
.BR MC1_HC_TUNNEL_PORT ;
default 8081.
.TP
.BI \-H " host"
Controller. Env
.BR MC1_HC_HOST ;
default
.BR mu2e-mc1-worker-01.fnal.gov .
.TP
.BI \-r " addr:port"
Site address on the controller. Env
.BR MC1_HC_REMOTE ;
default 127.0.0.1:80.
.TP
.B \-o
Open the browser
.RB ( open ,
.BR xdg-open " or " wslview )
when the site answers; the tunnel stays up until Ctrl-C.
.TP
.B \-c
Check only: open the tunnel, print the overall status and the checks that are
not ok, close the tunnel. Exit 0 ok, 1 warn, 2 fail or unreachable.
.TP
.B \-n
Print the ssh command and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
scripts/mc1-status-tunnel -o
scripts/mc1-status-tunnel -c            # quick look from a terminal
scripts/mc1-status-tunnel -p 9000 -u mu2edaq
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc1-healthcheck (1),
.BR ssh (1)
